# {{ title }}

Like `:::kanban`, these three directives are sugar for an implicit database rendered as a view — they exist so the view can be written as plain prose and still read as headings, lists or images in a tool that doesn't know them.

## Calendar

Every top-level list item is a card, placed by its `{due=...}`. There are no column headings, because a calendar groups by date, not by a named column.

:::calendar {title="October"}
- [ ] Submit grant report {due=2026-10-10}
- [ ] Team sync {due=2026-10-14 owner=ada}
- [ ] Draft budget review {due=2026-10-14 owner=grace}
:::

A card with no `{due=...}` isn't shown, and the linter reports `Y606`.

## Timeline

A calendar stretched into a bar: `{start=...}`/`{due=...}` are the start and end. Headings are optional — present, they group cards into lanes; absent, every card shares one track.

:::timeline {title="Q4 Roadmap"}
## Ada


## Alan

- [ ] Migrate auth {start=2026-11-10 due=2026-12-07}
- [ ] Ship billing API {start=2026-10-05 due=2026-10-19}
- [ ] Sign-up flow redesign {start=2026-10-22 due=2026-11-03}
:::

## Gallery

Each image starts a card; the paragraph(s) right after it (no blank line needed, since that's still the same paragraph) are its caption.

:::gallery {title="Trip photos"}
![Golden Gate Bridge](../assets/architecture.svg)
Shot at sunset from Battery Spencer. #landscape

![Yosemite Falls](../assets/architecture.svg)
Peak flow in spring. #landscape
:::

## Interacting in the preview

Each one gets the interaction its own shape calls for, not a copy of kanban's column-to-column drag:

- **Calendar** — drag a card to a different day to reschedule it (only its `{due=...}` changes; its line in the file doesn't move). Alt+Left/Right shifts by a day, Alt+Up/Down by a week. Click a card's title to expand its full detail (owner, tags, body) in place — clicking its checkbox still just ticks the task. Click a date or a week number to expand (or collapse) every card in that day or week at once.
- **Timeline** — drag a bar along its track to reschedule it (start and due shift together, so its length is kept); drag it onto a different lane's track to move it there. While dragging, a line and date label follow the cursor so you can see exactly where it'll land before you let go. Alt+Left/Right reschedules by a day, Alt+Up/Down moves to the neighboring lane.
- **Gallery** — drag a card to reorder it; Alt+Left/Right swaps it with a neighbor. The add-form takes two fields (image path, caption), since an image card has no single title to type.

Double-click a calendar or timeline card's title to rename it. Every one of these edits is a single undoable step and is saved automatically — no separate save, the way checking a task already worked.

## What's not sugar

A chart aggregates rows that already exist, so there's nothing to write as prose — there's no `:::chart`. Table and list already have a native plain-prose form (pipe tables and list tables), so they don't get one either. All of these are still reachable as `::db[...]` views over a real `.ydb` file.
